<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Anglo-Dutch War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1665–1667</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Dutch War</a> was a naval and colonial war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, fought from 1665 to 1667 over trade and overseas possessions. After English gains such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a> in 1664, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> won the Four Days' Battle, raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-medway">Medway</a> in 1667 and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>. The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breda">Breda</a> of 1667 left each side with what it held.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-anglo-dutch-war.jpg" alt="Second Anglo-Dutch War" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abraham Storck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Storck,_Four_Days_Battle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
